{"key": "KXEOWEEK|Will the President sign Executive Orders between Nov 2, 2025 and Nov 8, 2025?|If the President signs any Executive Orders during Nov 2, 2025 to Nov 8, 2025, then the market resolves to Yes. An Executive Order must be formally titled \"Executive Order\" followed by a number, signed by the President, and published in the Federal Register. Presidential Memoranda, Proclamations, Determinations, and other executive actions that are not formally numbered Executive Orders do not count. The signing date as recorded in the Federal Register determines which period an Executive Order belongs to, using ET timezone. Classified Executive Orders count if acknowledged by number. Executive Orders that are later revoked still count for the period they were signed. The Federal Register is the primary source; alternative sources are used only if the Federal Register explicitly states data is incomplete.", "decision": "YES", "confidence": 0.95, "reasoning": "Executive Order 14357 (\"Modifying Duties Addressing the Synthetic Opioid Supply Chain in the People's Republic of China\") was signed on November 4, 2025, which falls within the November 2-8, 2025 period specified in the resolution criteria. The order was formally titled as an Executive Order, signed by the President, and published in the Federal Register (Document 2025-19825 on November 7, 2025). This meets all the requirements of the resolution criteria: the order is formally numbered, was signed by the President during the specified window, and is documented in the Federal Register with the signing date recorded as November 4, 2025 (ET). Therefore, the market should resolve to YES.", "sources": ["https://www.presidency.ucsb.edu/documents/executive-order-14357-modifying-duties-addressing-the-synthetic-opioid-supply-chain-the", "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/11/07/2025-19825/modifying-duties-addressing-the-synthetic-opioid-supply-chain-in-the-peoples-republic-of-china", "https://www.whitehouse.go